 "verdict": "THE SEEDED SITE'S PHASE DECIDES THE OUTCOME, AND THE PHASE ONE PICKS MATTERS: the inflow a pair sees is F*(1+0.5*(2G-1)) at the site it is seeded at, so the nominal rate is only a site average. Across 376 runs in 17 cells where both outcomes occur, the pair's **midpoint** phase is anti-predictive of fusion (1 of the cells have the fused runs higher, mean point-biserial -0.561); among the 381 runs whose cell is not saturated the same reading holds (point-biserial -0.578; the bottom midpoint-G quartile fuses 88% against 14% in the top, z = -9.691, p = 0.0). X183 settles which phase is the informative one: the inflow at the **colder of the two bodies** organises the block's rate ladder (AUC 0.878 over the ladder, 0.898 within nominal levels, deviance 96.9 against 144.6 for the nominal rate), while the midpoint reading is anti-predictive (AUC 0.213). The midpoint table in this aggregate is kept as the record of why the phase question had to be asked."
}
